+### Session 072 — 2026-08-11 (Gate B CLEARED — reconciles Session 071)
+**Agent:** E2 Agent (Emergent, Neo)
+**Scope:** `S` (managed-database verification + one operator-approved schema migration + documentation; zero repository application/schema file changes)
+**Triggered by:** Operator supplied the managed Supabase `DATABASE_URL` and ran the full Gate B sequence in the Emergent continuation environment: read-only verification first, then a reviewed authorization packet, then an explicitly approved migration, then the clearance re-check.
+
+**Reconciliation with Session 071 (Replit environment):** Session 071's pooler attempt failed with `no tenant identifier provided` because it reused the direct-URI credential components (user `postgres`) against `aws-1-us-west-2`. This session confirmed the same root cause independently: `aws-1-us-west-2` rejected the proper pooler tenant too (`ENOTFOUND tenant/user`); the project's actual tenant-specific endpoint is **`aws-0-us-west-2.pooler.supabase.com:5432`** with pooler user `postgres.<project-ref>`, where authentication succeeded. Session 071's honest non-PASS disposition for its own run remains correct and untouched; this entry supersedes only the *gate status*.
+
+**What was done (all evidence in the Emergent workspace memory `GATE_B_RUN_2026-08-11.md`):**
+- **Run 1 — direct host:** BLOCKED by environment — direct host publishes only an AAAA (IPv6) record; container has zero IPv6 interfaces; raw TCP proof recorded. No local substitution; no fabricated result.
+- **Run 2 — operator-authorized session pooler (read-only):** connection PASS (session forced `transaction_read_only=on`); identity/version recorded (database `postgres`, **PostgreSQL 17.6**, UTF8, UTC, primary); **Supabase-managed CONFIRMED** (marker roles 3/3, marker schemas 4/4); extensions PASS (`pg_stat_statements`, `pgcrypto`, `plpgsql`, `supabase_vault`, `uuid-ossp`); migration state NONE (expected); catalog EMPTY → pinned comparison **0/18** = "schema absent — pending separately authorized migration". Honest interim verdict: environment VERIFIED, gate NOT CLEARED.
+- **Authorization packet (no execution):** exact non-secret target; same-tenant confirmation; pinned schema provenance (main `f17bdcec…` at packet time; schema dir tree `2c5feac6160deee7c4ce13496b0304f02eec0ea0`; source sha256 `2af45e443ff41e61ada7b1a7d7f130e9ba5ca561b60ebe55856e64ba79aeec37`; 18 tables); offline-generated full SQL plan (18 CREATE TABLE · 14 CREATE TYPE · 12 indexes · 34 FKs · **0 destructive statements**; plan sha256 `f765cf97bde2c89bd49c3e33b93c4d8012206bcc9cb42d4569d502e80ec39f67`); read-only writability confirmation. Held for explicit approval.
+- **Operator approval (verbatim scope):** "Create the 18 pinned OnCall Foot tables in the verified managed Supabase database — Option B approved" — excluding application changes, seed data, RLS, auth configuration, extra extensions, and the Race-Proof partial unique index.
+- **Option B execution:** plan hash re-verified programmatically (abort-on-mismatch), reviewed SQL applied byte-for-byte in ONE transaction — COMMITTED.
+- **Clearance re-check (read-only):** **18/18 pinned tables present, 0 absent, 0 unexpected — FULL MATCH**; scope audit exactly 14 enum types, 12 non-constraint indexes, 34 FKs, **0 rows** (no seed). **Independent verification: 16/16 checks passed** (separate testing agent; exact table-set match, object counts, structural spot-checks, read-only + rollback, secret hygiene).
+- Secret kept in a mode-600 env file outside the git tree; never printed, logged, committed, or patched. The lost pinned verifier (`df1465bb…`) was never reconstructed; all verifiers and hashes are new and clearly labeled.
+
+**Files changed:**
+- `.agents/LOG.md` (this entry)
+- `.agents/NEXT_TASK.md` (Priority 1 → CLEARED)
+
+**Build state at end:** **GATE B: CLEARED on an actual 18/18 result.** The managed Supabase database holds exactly the pinned OnCall Foot schema and nothing else (no data, no RLS, no auth config, no extra extensions, no race-proof index). Repository application and schema files untouched. Correct connection path for future runs: Supabase **Connect → Session pooler → URI** for this project (`aws-0-us-west-2`, tenant-bearing user), per `.agents/memory/supabase-session-pooler.md`.
+
+**Next best action:** (1) Race-Proof partial unique index on bookings as its own authorization + reviewed migration task (now unblocked); (2) managed-database seed policy decision through its own approval; (3) Phase 4C stack-native port PLAN (plan only). Activation phases / production event writes remain subject to their own approvals.
